    {
      "id": "sol.hmmt-feb-advanced-topics-1999-p7.hmmt",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The cube roots of 343 are the roots of \\(x^{3}-343\\), which is \\((x-7)\\left(x^{2}+7 x+49\\right)\\). Therefore the ordered pair we want is \\((\\mathbf{7}, 49)\\).",
